<title>USA: Omnicare Inc Q3 diluted shr $0.16 vs $0.12.</title>
<headline>Omnicare Inc Q3 diluted shr $0.16 vs $0.12.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended  Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>				    September 30,	 September 30,</p>
<p>				    1996   1995(a)     1996   1995(a)</p>
<p> Sales			$ 140,733$ 102,145$ 379,751$  289,797</p>
<p> Cost of sales		100,111   73,198  270,402   209,245</p>
<p> Gross profit		  40,622   28,947  109,349    80,552</p>
<p> Operating expenses	  23,213   16,789   63,285    48,751</p>
<p>Acquisition expenses -</p>
<p> pooling-of-interests (a)	 -	  -	  -  1,292(b)</p>
<p> Operating income	    17,409   12,158   46,064    30,509</p>
<p>   Fully Diluted	     78,303   65,660   74,423    65,074</p>
<p>			   Supplemental Pro Forma Data (unaudited):</p>
<p> Net income, as reported    $  11,813  6,935 $ 30,338  17,082</p>
<p>Acquisition expenses,</p>
<p>    net of taxes			  -	-	  -  989(b)</p>
<p> Pro forma net income	    11,813  6,935   30,338  18,071</p>
<p>Pro forma earnings per share (c):</p>
<p>   Primary			    0.17   0.13     0.48  0.35(b)</p>
<p>   Fully Diluted		    0.16   0.12     0.44  0.31(b)</p>
<p>Note:</p>
<p>(a) The 1995 year-to-date reflects the June 30, 1995 purchase of Specialized Pharmacy Services Inc in a pooling of interests transaction. As required by accounting rules for pooling of interests transactions, a charge to operating income for acquisition- related expenses was recorded in the quarter ended June 30, 1995.</p>
<p>(b) Acquisition expenses of $1,292,000 pretax, or $989,000 after taxes ($0.02 per primary share and $0.01 fully diluted), are included in the 1995 year-to-date period.  </p>
<p>Net income, excluding these acquisitions expenses, for the nine months ended September 30, 1995 was $18,071,000 ($0.35 per primiary share and $0.31 fully diluted), respectively (See Supplemental Pro Forma Data). (c) Adjusted for two-for-one stock split distributed June 27, 1996.</p>
<p>(000's except per share amounts)</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
